  <body>
    <header>
      <para styleclass="Heading1">SEEK Command &#160;(FoxPro)</para>
    </header>
    <para styleclass="Normal"><snippet src="__CommandInclude" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Purpose</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">Searches an indexed table for the first record whose index key matches the specified expression, optionally using a different order. This is the FoxPro version of the <link displaytype="text" defaultstyle="true" type="topiclink" href="command_SEEK">SEEK</link> command.</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Syntax</para>
    <para styleclass="Code with box">SEEK &lt;eExpression&gt; [ORDER [TAG] &lt;OrderName&gt; [OF &lt;IndexFile&gt;]] [ASCENDING | DESCENDING] [IN &lt;WorkArea&gt; | &lt;Alias&gt;]</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Arguments</para>
    <para styleclass="List">&lt;eExpression&gt;<tab />The value to search for.</para>
    <para styleclass="List">ORDER [TAG] &lt;OrderName&gt; [OF &lt;IndexFile&gt;]<tab />The order that is used for the search. The order that was active before the command was executed is restored afterwards.</para>
    <para styleclass="List">ASCENDING | DESCENDING<tab />The direction of the order that is used for the search.</para>
    <para styleclass="List"><snippet src="__In" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Remarks</para>
    <para styleclass="Normal">After the command the function Found() returns TRUE when a matching record was found. When no matching record was found, then the record pointer is positioned at the end of the file (or at the next higher key when SET SOFTSEEK is ON).</para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">Examples</para>
    <para styleclass="Code Example">USE Customers<br/>
SEEK "Smith" ORDER TAG LastName<br/>
IF Found()<br/>
&#160; ? Name<br/>
ENDIF</para>
    <para styleclass="Body Text"><snippet src="__IncludeLibVFP" inline="false"/></para>
    <para styleclass="Heading1">See Also</para>
